1422 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Art travels with people\056 \nWhen artists migrate\054 they carry their craft across borders\054 transforming local traditions into global forms\056 Cultural diaspora captures this process\054 tracing how human mobility shapes the spread and evolution of cultural expressions across time and place\056 \nBallet is one of the most striking examples\054 a European elite art that became a worldwide cultural force through centuries of migration\054 exchange\054 and reinvention\056)
     /K [ 8 ]
     /P 1423 0 R
     /Pg 1406 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1423 0 obj
  << /K [ 1422 0 R ]
     /P 1446 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1406 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1424 0 obj
  << /ActualText (DATA AND METHODS \nWe use LLMs to convert narrative entries from Wikipedia into structured records\056 Our goal is to test if Wikipedia can be reliably used to extract structured information about artistic mobility\054 as a starting point for the systematic study of cultural diaspora\056)
     /K [ 9 ]
     /P 1425 0 R
     /Pg 1406 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1425 0 obj
  << /K [ 1424 0 R ]
     /P 1446 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1406 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1426 0 obj
  << /ActualText (We scrape 518 ballet entries from Wikipedia\047s List of Ballets by Title\054 then we use GPT\0553\0565 and GPT\0554 to extract named artists\054 creative roles\054 and premiere cities from each entry\056 )
     /K [ 10 ]
     /P 1427 0 R
     /Pg 1406 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1427 0 obj
  << /K [ 1426 0 R ]
     /P 1446 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1406 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1428 0 obj
  << /ActualText (NETWORK CONSTRUCTION \nThe structured data enabled the construction of the artists collaboration network based on the geographic location of their work\072 )
     /K [ 11 ]
     /P 1429 0 R
     /Pg 1406 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1429 0 obj
  << /K [ 1428 0 R ]
     /P 1446 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1406 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1430 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Each artist is represented as a node\054 and two artists are connected if they share a premiere city\056 This geographic co\055location serves as a proxy for artistic exchange and creative mobility across borders\056)
     /K [ 12 ]
     /P 1431 0 R
     /Pg 1406 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1431 0 obj
  << /K [ 1430 0 R ]
     /P 1446 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1406 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1432 0 obj
  << /ActualText (NETWORK ANALYSIS \nWe analyze the structure of the artists network using connectivity and component analysis to assess cohesion across borders\054 and identify key nodes that bridge creative communities across countries\056 )
     /K [ 13 ]
     /P 1433 0 R
     /Pg 1406 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1433 0 obj
  << /K [ 1432 0 R ]
     /P 1446 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1406 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1434 0 obj
  << /ActualText (The LLM structuring yields 1\054042 artist records spanning six roles\072 composers\054 choreographers\054 designers\054 muses\054 librettists\054 and regisseurs\056 Roles are compiled into a structured dataset and validated against a manually verified subset\056)
     /K [ 14 ]
     /P 1435 0 R
     /Pg 1406 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

